s/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":92,"digest":"sha256:4dd60474ee3fc1444ae641535f6bb18375d1b5634d146a5ccd2b8784258323e8","download_count":4,"created_at":"2026-10-29T19:18:37Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T19:18:37Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/Oliv3rmoon/Nightshade/releases/download/v1.010.002/SHA256SUMS"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Oliv3rmoon/Nightshade/tarball/v1.010.002","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Oliv3rmoon/Nightshade/zipball/v1.010.002","body":"**The likely cause of Final Fantasy Resonance stopping the GPU, fixed: draws made from arguments the GPU hadn't finished writing.** Every stop in Oliv3rmoon/Nightshade#1, in the opening scene and after it, came right after draws asking for 27 million to 2 billion copies of a model (one count read as the float 1.0): far more than any game draws, so the GPU ran them until it was reset. Not confirmed on a console yet.\n\n### Fixes\n\n- **Draw arguments the GPU wrote are read once its newest write is in memory.** Some games have the GPU work out how many copies of a model to draw. Eden marks memory the GPU wrote so it fetches it before the CPU reads it, but a fetch that finished could clear the mark of a range the GPU had written again since, and Eden then took the older contents as current. Such a range now stays marked until its newest contents arrive (Eden patch 11). The `submit_sync` switch made this rarer by waiting for the GPU after every submission; it is no longer needed for it.\n- **Arguments that came from GPU memory are read again before use at every accuracy level**, not only at High.\n- **A draw that can't be real is dropped instead of stopping the GPU.** If a draw the CPU makes from such arguments still asks for more than about 4 billion vertices after they are read again, Nightshade skips it and says so in `stderr.log` (`EDEN_INDIRECT_DRAW_DROPPED`).\n\n### For testing a game that stops the GPU\n\n- **The stall report shows an indirect draw's arguments** (its count and copies, and how many draws a multi draw makes), read from memory, so a stop on a draw the GPU makes itself shows whether its arguments were wrong too.\n\n### Install\n\nFrom 1.005.102 or later, **Update now** applies it. If it doesn't, send `/data/prosperoeden/logs/updater.log`. From an older version, copy this ZIP's `PPSA99008` folder over yours.\n"}